From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] libarchive: the xar stub calls the entitlement check by its name

Without an XML parser (no libxml2, expat or bsdxml), the xar reader
compiles to a stub that reports the format unsupported. Apple's builds
always have libxml2, so the stub's entitlement check, which calls
archive_allow_format(), a name archive_check_entitlement.h doesn't
declare, has never been compiled. It calls
archive_allow_entitlement_format(), as the reader proper does.
NeoDarwin's base has no libxml2 (nd_libarchive_config.h).
Rebase-risk: low (one line).

--- a/libarchive/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_xar.c
+++ b/libarchive/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_xar.c
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 	struct archive_read *a = (struct archive_read *)_a;
 
 #ifdef __APPLE__
-	if (!archive_allow_format("xar")) {
+	if (!archive_allow_entitlement_format("xar")) {
 		archive_set_error(_a, ARCHIVE_ERRNO_MISC, "Format not allow-listed in entitlements");
 		return ARCHIVE_FATAL;
 	}
